  "implemented": [
    "Private D01 inline-atoms operations carry retained paragraph addresses, exact text-gap before-values, complete target AST, and registered atom bindings. Pure decoding reconstructs all intentions and rejects altered paths, locations, widths, fallbacks, missing records and mismatched skeleton text.",
    "New native math, mentions and sources materialize in retained paragraphs after their ordinary text/mark/link edits. The canonical paragraph, properties and enclosing table or heading remain native.",
    "Existing unchanged controls anchor right-to-left text gaps. Later text edits and new atom births preserve original native control IDs, exact control fingerprints and payload metadata. Equal literal source attributes can reorder without rewriting the control.",
    "Gap extraction visits selected AST paths rather than scanning the whole paragraph for every gap. Repeated equal atoms pair by ordinal only when counts agree; unresolved ambiguous identities refuse.",
    "Both client orders and reconnect receivers preserve same-paragraph peer edits through atom insertion, undo/redo, exact Word fingerprints, imported OMML, remote caret geometry and DOCX/room reopening.",
    "A stronger isolated/compiled case edits newly inserted ordinary text while the inserting actor undoes. The peer text survives atom removal and redo, with both independent actor histories.",
    "New block identities are unique across every operation, including retained atoms, sibling blocks/atoms and row/column/split payload births. Mixed or repeated identities refuse before package publication or history changes."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Image resource resolution and source projection, reference/media provenance, and media allocation only for new image bytes.",
    "Atoms in new rows or columns of existing tables.",
    "Linked/code-marked atom insertion, hyperlink reconciliation around retained controls, and unresolved repeated-atom ambiguity.",
    "Tracked inline birth ownership, accept/reject retirement, source scope reconciliation and same-payload concurrent fields.",
    "Installed application SDK cutover and browser feature parity."
  ],
